\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 2. BIOGRAPHY (ENGLISH)
\fs24 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-5\sl360\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 Mishka Adams is a Filipina/English award-winning singer, multi-instrumentalist, vocal arranger and vocal ensemble leader now based in Buenos Aires, Argentina. She works in a variety of different projects that draw from styles and rhythms of Latin America, primarily Brazil, Argentina and Uruguay. She also sings as a soloist in her project of original songs, with influences closer to her musical beginnings in jazz and folk. She has recorded 9 albums to date and has another album and an EP in the making.\
\
Her most recent collaborative projects include her duo with her husband 
\f0\b Beto Caletti
\f1\b0 , a singer/guitarist/composer renowned for his work with Brazilian music; 
\f0\b Canciones Migrantes
\f1\b0  with Florencia D\'e1valos and Georgina Hassan, a vocal trio bringing together songs of immigration from all over the world; 
\f0\b Cantoras del Sur
\f1\b0 , a vocal octet with percussion and accordion, and 
\f0\b Mujerer\'edo Voces y Cuerpo
\f1\b0 , an acapella nonet.\
\
Before moving to Buenos Aires, she signed a four-album record deal with Candid Records in 2004 and in 2006 moved to London to study jazz. She lived there for many years, with a strong presence in the jazz and Brazilian music scene with her solo project and various collaborations and groups. In 2007 she co-founded the 
\f0\b \'93London Vocal Project\'94
\f1\b0  with close friend and teacher Pete Churchill and was a vocalist and percussionist in the renowned samba group 
\f0\b \'93Rhythms of the City\'94
\f1\b0 .\
\
She has played and toured extensively worldwide but is also passionate about teaching \'96she has 20 years of teaching experience and directs two female choirs and also gives one to one lessons in voice and percussion for singers.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-5\sl360\partightenfactor0

